2078:
**ἔσχατος**, -η, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחֲרִית אַחֲרוֹן ;] 
**last, utmost, extreme**; 
(a) **of place**: of the lowest or least honoured place, [[42-luke.14.9|Luk.14:9-10;]] τ. ἔσχατον, with genitive part., [[44-acts.1.8|Act.1:8 13:47]]; 
(b) **of time**: [[40-matthew.20.12|Mat.20:12, 14]], [[41-mark.12.6|Mrk.12:6, 22]], opposite to πρῶτος, [[40-matthew.20.8|Mat.20:8]], [[46-1-corinthians.15.45|1Co.15:45]], [[66-revelation.2.19|Rev.2:19]], al.; τὰ ἔ. καὶ T. πρῶτα, [[40-matthew.12.45|Mat.12:45]], [[42-luke.11.26|Luk.11:26]], [[61-2-peter.2.20|2Pe.2:20]]; of the Eternal, ὁ πρῶτος καὶ ὁ ἔ., [[66-revelation.1.17|Rev.1:17 2:8 22:13]]; in phrases relating to the Messianic age and the consummation of the Kingdom of God: ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάτου (-ων) τ. ἡμερῶν, [[58-hebrews.1.2|Heb.1:2]], [[61-2-peter.3.3|2Pe.3:3]]; τ. χρόνων, [[60-1-peter.1.20|1Pe.1:20;]] ἔ. ὥρα, [[62-1-john.2.18|1Jn.2:18;]] ἐπ᾽ ἐ. χόνου, Ju 18; ἐν ἐ. ἡμέραις, [[44-acts.2.17|Act.2:17]], [[59-james.5.3|Jas.5:3]], [[55-2-timothy.3.1|2Ti.3:1]]; neut., ἔσχατον, as adv., [[41-mark.12.22|Mrk.12:22]], [[46-1-corinthians.15.8|1Co.15:8]]; 
(with) **of rank**: [[41-mark.9.35|Mrk.9:35]], [[46-1-corinthians.4.9|1Co.4:9]] 
(AS)

2087:
**ἕτερος**, -α, -ον, 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחֵר ;] 
_distributive pron._, prop. dual (BL, §13, 5; 51, 6), denoting the second of a pair, but in late Gk. encroaching on ἄλλος (M, _Pr._, 79f.); 
1. of number, **other**; with art., **the other**; 
(a) of two, [[42-luke.5.7|Luk.5:7 9:56]], al.; opposite to ὁ πρῶτος, [[40-matthew.21.30|Mat.21:30;]] ὁ εἷς, [[40-matthew.6.24|Mat.6:24]], [[42-luke.7.41|Luk.7:41]], [[44-acts.23.6|Act.23:6]], al.; ἕ. μὲν . . . ἕ. δέ, **the one . . . the other**: [[46-1-corinthians.15.40|1Co.15:40;]] **the next**: [[42-luke.6.6|Luk.6:6 9:56]] (sc. ἡμέρα, Xen.), [[44-acts.20.15|Act.20:15 27:3]]; = ὁ πλησίον, **one's neighbour**: [[45-romans.2.1|Rom.2:1 13:8]], [[46-1-corinthians.6.1|1Co.6:1]], al.; 
(b) of more than two, **another**: [[40-matthew.8.21|Mat.8:21 11:3]], [[42-luke.6.6|Luk.6:6 22:65]], [[43-john.19.37|Jhn.19:37]], [[45-romans.8.39|Rom.8:39]], al.; pl., [[44-acts.2.13|Act.2:13;]] οἱ μὲν . . . ἄλλοι δὲ . . . ἕ. δέ, [[40-matthew.16.14|Mat.16:14;]] τινὲς . . . ἕ. δέ, [[42-luke.11.16|Luk.11:16.]] 
2. Of kind or quality, **other, another, different** (Plat., Dem., al.): Mrk.16:[12], [[42-luke.9.29|Luk.9:29]], [[44-acts.2.4|Act.2:4]], [[46-1-corinthians.14.21|1Co.14:21]], [[47-2-corinthians.11.4|2Co.11:4]], [[48-galatians.1.6|Gal.1:6]], al. (cf. ἑτερό-γλωσσος, -διδασκαλέω, -ζυγέω). 
_SYN._: ἄλλος, which see (see reff. ut supr., also Robertson, _Gr._, 748ff.). (AS)

2089:
**ἔτι **
_adv._, 
**yet, as yet, still**; 
1. **of time**; 
(a) **of the present **(adhuc): [[41-mark.5.35|Mrk.5:35]], [[46-1-corinthians.3.3|1Co.3:3 15:17]], [[48-galatians.1.10|Gal.1:10]], al.; 
(b) of the past, mostly with impf.: [[40-matthew.12.46|Mat.12:46]], [[42-luke.8.49|Luk.8:49 15:20]], [[43-john.20.1|Jhn.20:1]], [[44-acts.9.1|Act.9:1]], [[45-romans.5.6|Rom.5:6]], 8, [[53-2-thessalonians.2.5|2Th.2:5]], [[58-hebrews.7.10|Heb.7:10 9:8]], al.; 
(with) **of the future**: [[42-luke.1.15|Luk.1:15]], [[47-2-corinthians.1.10|2Co.1:10]]; 
(d) with a neg.: [[40-matthew.5.13|Mat.5:13]], [[42-luke.16.2|Luk.16:2 20:36]], [[58-hebrews.10.2|Heb.10:2]], [[66-revelation.3.12|Rev.3:12 20:3]], al. 
2. **Of degree, even, yet, still, further**: with compar., [[50-philippians.1.9|Php.1:9]], [[58-hebrews.7.15|Heb.7:15]]; of what remains, [[41-mark.12.6|Mrk.12:6]], [[43-john.4.35|Jhn.4:35 7:33]], al.; of what is added, [[40-matthew.18.16|Mat.18:16 26:65]], [[58-hebrews.11.32|Heb.11:32 12:26-27]]; of con­tinuance apart from the idea of time, [[45-romans.3.7|Rom.3:7 6:2 9:19]], [[48-galatians.5.11|Gal.5:11]]; ἔτι δἐ, [[44-acts.2.26|Act.2:26]] (LXX), [[58-hebrews.11.36|Heb.11:36;]] ἔτι τε καί, [[42-luke.14.26|Luk.14:26]], [[44-acts.21.28|Act.21:28]] 
(AS)

2099:
**εὐαγγελιστής**, -οῦ, ὁ 
**an evangelist**; 
(a) in NT, a preacher of the gospel: [[44-acts.21.8|Act.21:8]], [[49-ephesians.4.11|Eph.4:11]], [[55-2-timothy.4.5|2Ti.4:5]]; 
(b) later, a writer of a gospel (eccl.).
(AS)

2106:
**εὐ-δοκέω**, -ῶ
(on the derivation, see EL, § 28, 6) [in LXX chiefly for רָצָה, also for אָבָה, חָפֵץ, etc. ;] 
1. with inf. (Polyb., al.), **to be well pleased, to think it good, to give consent **(so frequently in π. in legal docu­ments; Milligan, _Th._, 22 f.): [[42-luke.12.32|Luk.12:32]], [[45-romans.15.26|Rom.15:26-27]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.21|1Co.1:21]], [[48-galatians.1.15|Gal.1:15]], [[51-colossians.1.19|Col.1:19]], R, mg. (_ICC_, in l, but see infr.), [[52-1-thessalonians.2.8|1Th.2:8 3:1]]; μᾶλλον εὐ., [[47-2-corinthians.5.8|2Co.5:8;]] with accusative and inf. (Polyb., i, 8, 4), Col, l.with, R, txt. (Lft., in l). 
2. **to be well pleased or take pleasure with or in a person or thing**; 
(a) with dative (Polyb., al.; 1Ma.1:43, I [[17-esther.4.39|Est.4:39]]): [[53-2-thessalonians.2.12|2Th.2:12]]; 
(b) as frequently in LXX, 
α with accusative: [[40-matthew.12.13|Mat.12:13]], [[58-hebrews.10.5|Heb.10:5]], 8" (LXX) ; 
β before ἐν (cf. _Heb._ בּ רָצָה, [[19-psalms.149.4|Psa.149:4]]): [[40-matthew.3.17|Mat.3:17 17:5]], [[41-mark.1.11|Mrk.1:11]], [[42-luke.3.22|Luk.3:22]] (on the tense, see M, _Pr._, 134 f.; _DCG_, i,308 b), [[46-1-corinthians.10.5|1Co.10:5]], [[47-2-corinthians.12.10|2Co.12:10]], [[58-hebrews.10.38|Heb.10:38]]" (LXX) ; 
(with) before εἰς: [[61-2-peter.1.17|2Pe.1:17.]] (cf. συν-ευδοκέω, and see Cremer, 213 f.; Field, _Notes_, 48 f.; _DCG_, i, 355a.)
(AS)

2128:
**εὐλογητός**, -όν
(εὐλογέω), [in LXX chiefly for בָּרַךְ ;] 
**blessed**; 
(a) of men ([[01-genesis.12.2|Gen.12:2]] A, [[05-deuteronomy.7.14|Deu.7:14]], [[07-judges.17.2|Jdg.17:2]] B, [[08-ruth.2.20|Rut.2:20]], [[09-1-samuel.15.13|1Ki.15:13]]); 
(b) of God (Lft., _Notes_, 310 f.), as chiefly in LXX ([[01-genesis.9.26|Gen.9:26]], [[02-exodus.17.10|Exo.17:10]], [[19-psalms.18.46|Psa.18:46]], al.): [[42-luke.1.68|Luk.1:68]], [[45-romans.1.25|Rom.1:25 9:5]] (_ICC_, in l), [[47-2-corinthians.1.3|2Co.1:3 11:31]], [[49-ephesians.1.3|Eph.1:3]], [[60-1-peter.1.3|1Pe.1:3]]; absol., ὁ εὐλογητός (Dalman, _Words_, 200; JThS, v, 453), [[41-mark.14.61|Mrk.14:61]] (Cremer, 769).
(AS)

2186:
**ἐφ-ίστημι **
[in LXX for נָצַב ni., שִׁית, נָתַן, etc. ;] 
1. causal in pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., to set upon or by, set up, etc. (Æsch., Hdt., Arist., al). 
2. Intrans. in mid, and in pf. and 2 aor. act.; 
(a) **to stand upon**; 
(b) **to be set over**; 
(with) **to stand by, be present, be at hand, come on or upon**: [[42-luke.2.38|Luk.2:38 10:40 20:1]], [[44-acts.6.12|Act.6:12 12:7 22:13, 20 23:27]], [[55-2-timothy.4.2|2Ti.4:2]]; with dative pars., [[42-luke.2.9|Luk.2:9 24:4]], [[44-acts.4.1|Act.4:1 23:11]]; with dative bc., [[44-acts.17.5|Act.17:5;]] before έπί, with accusative, [[44-acts.10.17|Act.10:17 11:11]]; of rain, [[44-acts.28.2|Act.28:2;]] of evils impending, with dative of person(s), [[52-1-thessalonians.5.3|1Th.5:3;]] before έπί (Wis.6:9), [[42-luke.21.34|Luk.21:34]]; of time, [[55-2-timothy.4.6|2Ti.4:6]] (cf. κατ-, συν-εφίστημι).
(AS)

2192:
**ἔχω**, 
[in LXX for אָצֵל (ἐχόμενος), יֵשׁ,בַּעַל, etc., 59 words in all ;] 
(on the _Aktionsart_ of the various tenses, see M, _Pr._, 110, 145, 150, 183), **to have**, as in cl., in various senses and constructions. 
I. Trans.; 
1. 1. **to have, hold, hold fast**, etc.; 
(a) **to hold**, **as, in the hand**: [[66-revelation.5.8|Rev.5:8 14:6]], al.; ἐν τ. χειρί, [[66-revelation.1.16|Rev.1:16 10:2]], al.; 
(b) of arms and clothing, = φέρω, φορέω, **to bear, wear**: [[40-matthew.3.4|Mat.3:4 22:12]], al.; so frequently present ptcp. (LS, see word, A, I, 6; Bl., 74, 2), [[41-mark.11.13|Mrk.11:13]], [[43-john.18.10|Jhn.18:10]], [[66-revelation.9.17|Rev.9:17]], al.; 
(with) of a woman, ἐν γαστρὶ ἔ, **to be with child**: [[41-mark.13.17|Mrk.13:17]], [[45-romans.9.10|Rom.9:10]]; 
(d) **to hold fast, keep**: [[42-luke.19.20|Luk.19:20;]] metaphorically, of the mind and conduct, [[41-mark.16.8|Mrk.16:8]] (cf. [[18-job.21.6|Job.21:6]], [[23-isaiah.13.8|Isa.13:8]]; Deiss., _BS_, 293; Field, _Notes_, 44f.), [[43-john.14.21|Jhn.14:21]], [[45-romans.1.28|Rom.1:28]], [[54-1-timothy.3.9|1Ti.3:9]], [[55-2-timothy.1.13|2Ti.1:13]], [[66-revelation.6.9|Rev.6:9]], al.; 
(e) **to involve**: [[58-hebrews.10.35|Heb.10:35]] (LXX), [[59-james.1.4|Jas.1:4]], [[62-1-john.4.18|1Jn.4:18;]] (_f_) = Lat. habere (Bl., §34, 5; 73, 5), **to hold, consider**: with accusative and predic. ptcp., [[42-luke.14.18|Luk.14:18;]] with accusative, before ὡς, [[40-matthew.14.5|Mat.14:5;]] εἰς (Hebraism), [[40-matthew.21.46|Mat.21:46;]] on (Bl., §70, 2), [[41-mark.11.32|Mrk.11:32.]] 
2. **to have, possess**; 
(a) in general, with accusative of thing(s): [[40-matthew.19.22|Mat.19:22]], [[41-mark.10.22|Mrk.10:22]], [[42-luke.12.19|Luk.12:19]], [[43-john.10.16|Jhn.10:16]], [[46-1-corinthians.11.22|1Co.11:22]], al.; of wealth or poverty, absol., ἔχειν (neg. οὐκ, μή), [[40-matthew.13.12|Mat.13:12 25:29]], [[47-2-corinthians.8.12|2Co.8:12]]; ἐκ τ. ἔχειν, **according to your means**, [[47-2-corinthians.8.11|2Co.8:11;]] 
(b) of relationship, association, and: πατέρα, [[43-john.8.41|Jhn.8:41;]] γυναῖκα (MM, xiv), [[46-1-corinthians.7.2|1Co.7:2;]] φίλον, [[42-luke.11.5|Luk.11:5;]] βασιλέα, [[43-john.19.15|Jhn.19:15;]] ποιμένα, [[40-matthew.9.36|Mat.9:36;]] with dupl. accusative, [[40-matthew.3.9|Mat.3:9]], al.; 
(with) **of parts or members**: ὦτα, [[40-matthew.19.15|Mat.19:15;]] μέλη, [[45-romans.12.4|Rom.12:4;]] θεμελίους, 
(d) with accusative, as periphrasis of verb: μνεῖαν ἔ. (= μεμνῆσθαι), [[52-1-thessalonians.3.6|1Th.3:6;]] ἀγάπην, [[43-john.13.35|Jhn.13:35;]] γνῶσιν, [[46-1-corinthians.8.1|1Co.8:1;]] πεποίθησιν, [[47-2-corinthians.3.4|2Co.3:4;]] θλίψιν, [[43-john.16.33|Jhn.16:33]], etc. (Thayer, see word, I, 2, f., g.); 
(e) of duty, necessity, etc.: ἀνάγκην, [[46-1-corinthians.7.37|1Co.7:37;]] νόμον, [[43-john.19.7|Jhn.19:7;]] ἐπιταγήν, [[46-1-corinthians.7.25|1Co.7:25;]] ἀγῶνα, [[50-philippians.1.30|Php.1:30;]] κρίμα, [[54-1-timothy.5.12|1Ti.5:12;]] 
(f) **of complaints and disputes**; κατά, with genitive of person(s), [[40-matthew.5.23|Mat.5:23]], [[41-mark.11.25|Mrk.11:25]]; id. before ὅτι, [[66-revelation.2.4|Rev.2:4, 20]]; with accusative before πρός, [[44-acts.24.19|Act.24:19]], al.; 
(g) with inf., 
(α) (cl.) **to be able** (Field, _Notes_, 14): [[40-matthew.18.25|Mat.18:25]], [[41-mark.14.8|Mrk.14:8]] (sc. ποιῆσαι), [[42-luke.12.4|Luk.12:4]], [[44-acts.4.14|Act.4:14]], al; 
(β) **of necessity **(BL, §69, 4): [[42-luke.12.50|Luk.12:50]], [[44-acts.23.17|Act.23:17-19 28:19]].
II. Intrans. (BL, §53, 1), **to be in a certain condition**: ἑτοίμως ἔ., with inf., [[44-acts.21.13|Act.21:13]], [[47-2-corinthians.12.14|2Co.12:14]]; ἐσχάτως (which see), [[41-mark.5.23|Mrk.5:23;]] κακῶς, **to be ill**, [[40-matthew.4.24|Mat.4:24]], al.; καλῶς, Mk 16:[18]; κομψότερον, [[43-john.4.52|Jhn.4:52;]] πῶς, [[44-acts.15.36|Act.15:36;]] impers., ἄλλως εἴχει, **it is otherwise**, [[54-1-timothy.5.25|1Ti.5:25;]] οὕτως, [[44-acts.7.1|Act.7:1]], al.; τὸ νῦν ἔχον, **as things now are** (Tob.7:11), [[44-acts.24.25|Act.24:25]]. 
III. Mid., -ομαι, **to hold oneself fast, hold on** or **cling to, be next to**: with genitive, τ. ἐχόμενα σωτηρίας, [[58-hebrews.6.9|Heb.6:9]] (Rendall, in l.); ptcp., ὁ ἐχόμενος, **near, next**: of place, [[41-mark.1.38|Mrk.1:38;]] of time, τ. ἐχομένη (ἡμέρα, expressed or understood), [[42-luke.13.33|Luk.13:33]], [[44-acts.20.15|Act.20:15 21:26]]; (σαββάτῳ), [[44-acts.13.44|Act.13:44.]] (Cf. ἀν-, προσ-αν-, ἀντ-, ἀπ-, ἐν-, ἐπ-, κατ-, μετ-, παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-, ὑπερ-, ὑπ-έχω.) 
(AS)

2193:
**ἕως**, 
_relative particle_ (Lat. _donee, usque), _ 
expressing the terminus ad quem (cf. Burton, §321ff.). 
I. As _conjunction_; 
1. **till, until**; 
(a) of a fact in past time, with indic.: [[40-matthew.2.9|Mat.2:9]], al. (Wis.10:14, al.); 
(b) ἕως ἄν, with subjc. aor.: [[40-matthew.2.13|Mat.2:13 5:18]], [[41-mark.6.10|Mrk.6:10]], al.; without ἄν (M. _Pr._, 168f.; Lft., _Notes_, 115), [[41-mark.14.32|Mrk.14:32]] (Burton, §325), [[42-luke.12.59|Luk.12:59]], [[53-2-thessalonians.2.7|2Th.2:7]], al.; 
(with) with indic., present (Burton, §328; BL, §65, 10): [[41-mark.6.45|Mrk.6:45]], [[43-john.21.22|Jhn.21:22, 23]] [[54-1-timothy.4.13|1Ti.4:13]]. 
2. C. indic., **as long as, while** (Burton, §327): [[43-john.9.4|Jhn.9:4]] (Plat., Phaedo, 89c). 
II. As an _adverb_ (chiefly in late writers). 
1. Of time, **until, unto**; 
(a) as _prep._ with genitive (BL, §40, 6; M, _Pr._, 99): τ. ἡμέρας, [[40-matthew.26.29|Mat.26:29]], [[42-luke.1.80|Luk.1:80]], [[45-romans.11.8|Rom.11:8]], al.; ὥρας, [[40-matthew.27.45|Mat.27:45]], al.; τέλους, [[46-1-corinthians.1.8|1Co.1:8]], [[47-2-corinthians.1.13|2Co.1:13]]; τ. νῦν, [[40-matthew.24.21|Mat.24:21]], [[41-mark.13.19|Mrk.13:19]] (1Ma.2:33); ἐτῶν ὀγ. (Field, _Notes_, 49f.), [[42-luke.2.37|Luk.2:37;]] τ. ἐλθεῖν, [[44-acts.8.40|Act.8:40;]] before names and events, [[40-matthew.1.17|Mat.1:17 2:15]], [[42-luke.11.51|Luk.11:51]], [[59-james.5.7|Jas.5:7]], al.; 
(b) before οὗ, ὅτου, with the force of a _conjc._ (Burton, §330; M, _Pr._, 91); 
(α) ἕ. οὗ (Hdt., ii, 143; Plut., al.): with indic., [[40-matthew.1.25|Mat.1:25]] (WH br., οὗ) 13:33, al.; with subjc. aor., [[40-matthew.14.22|Mat.14:22]], al.; 
(β) ἔ. ὅτου: with subjc., [[42-luke.13.8|Luk.13:8;]] with indic., [[40-matthew.5.25|Mat.5:25]] (**until**), [[43-john.9.18|Jhn.9:18;]] 
(with) with _adv._ (ἔ. ὀψέ, Thuc, iii, 108): ἄρτι, [[40-matthew.11.12|Mat.11:12]], [[43-john.2.10|Jhn.2:10]], [[46-1-corinthians.4.13|1Co.4:13]], al.; πότε (M, _Pr._, 107), [[40-matthew.17.17|Mat.17:17]], [[41-mark.9.19|Mrk.9:19]], [[43-john.10.24|Jhn.10:24]], al. 
2. Of place, **as far as, even to, unto** (Arist., al.); 
(a) as _prep._ with genitive (see supr.): Mt 1123, Lk 1015, al.; 
(b) with _adv._ (BL, §40, 6): ἄνω, [[43-john.2.7|Jhn.2:7;]] ἔσω, [[41-mark.14.54|Mrk.14:54;]] κάτω, [[40-matthew.27.51|Mat.27:51]], [[41-mark.15.38|Mrk.15:38]]; ὧδε, [[42-luke.23.5|Luk.23:5;]] 
(with) with _prep._: ἔξω, [[44-acts.21.5|Act.21:5;]] πρός, [[42-luke.24.50|Luk.24:50]] (Field, _Notes_, 83). 
3. Of quantity, measure, etc.: [[40-matthew.18.21|Mat.18:21]], [[41-mark.6.23|Mrk.6:23]], [[42-luke.22.51|Luk.22:51]], al. 
(AS)

2228:
**ἤ**, 
_disjunctive and comparative particle_ (Bl., §36, 12; 77, 11); 
1. disjunctive, **or**; 
(a) **between single words**: [[40-matthew.5.17|Mat.5:17]] [[41-mark.6.56|Mrk.6:56]], [[42-luke.2.24|Luk.2:24]], [[43-john.6.19|Jhn.6:19]], [[45-romans.1.21|Rom.1:21]], al.; 
(b) before a sentence expressing a variation, denial or refutation of a previous statement, frequently in interrog. form: [[40-matthew.7.4|Mat.7:4]], 9 [[41-mark.12.14|Mrk.12:14]], [[42-luke.13.4|Luk.13:4]], [[45-romans.3.29|Rom.3:29 6:3 9:21]], [[46-1-corinthians.6.9|1Co.6:9]], 16 9:6, [[47-2-corinthians.11.7|2Co.11:7;]] ἤ . . . ἤ, **either . . . or**, [[40-matthew.6.24|Mat.6:24]], [[42-luke.16.13|Luk.16:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.14.6|1Co.14:6]]; 
(with) **in a disjunctive question **(as Lat. an after utrum): [[40-matthew.9.5|Mat.9:5]], [[41-mark.2.9|Mrk.2:9]], [[42-luke.7.19|Luk.7:19]], al.; after πότερον, [[43-john.7.17|Jhn.7:17;]] μή, [[46-1-corinthians.9.8|1Co.9:8;]] μήτι, [[47-2-corinthians.1.17|2Co.1:17;]] ἤ . . . ἤ . . . ἤ, [[41-mark.13.35|Mrk.13:35.]] 
2. Comparative, **than**: after comparatives, [[40-matthew.10.15|Mat.10:15]], [[42-luke.9.13|Luk.9:13]], [[43-john.3.19|Jhn.3:19]], [[45-romans.13.11|Rom.13:11]], al.; after ἕτερον, [[44-acts.17.21|Act.17:21;]] θέλω (Khüner 3, iv, 303), [[46-1-corinthians.14.19|1Co.14:19;]] πρὶν ἤ, **before**, before accusative and inf., [[40-matthew.1.18|Mat.1:18]] [[41-mark.14.30|Mrk.14:30]]; after a positive adj. ([[01-genesis.49.12|Gen.49:12;]] cf. Robertson, _Gr._, 661), [[40-matthew.18.8|Mat.18:8]], 9 [[41-mark.9.43|Mrk.9:43, 45]] 47. 
