2398:
**ἴδιος**, -α, -ον (in Attic usually -ος, -ον), 
[in LXX chiefly for of person(s) suff., also for לָהֶם, etc.; (τὰ ἴ.) בֵּיתוֹ ;] 
1. **one's own**; 
(a) **of that which is private and personal **(in cl. opposite to κοινός, δημόσιος; cf. infr. 3); 
(b) of property, friends, home, country, etc. (in cl. opposite to ἀλλότριος; in late writers often, like ἑαυτοῦ, with weakened sense, see M, _Pr._, 87ff.; Deiss., _BS_, 123f.): [[42-luke.6.41|Luk.6:41]], [[43-john.1.42|Jhn.1:42 5:43]], [[44-acts.2.6|Act.2:6 20:28]], [[46-1-corinthians.11.21|1Co.11:21]], [[48-galatians.6.5|Gal.6:5]], [[55-2-timothy.1.9|2Ti.1:9]], [[58-hebrews.7.27|Heb.7:27]], Ju 6, al.; πράσσειν τὰ ἴ., [[52-1-thessalonians.4.11|1Th.4:11;]] κατὰ τὰς ἰ. ἐπιθυμίας, [[55-2-timothy.4.3|2Ti.4:3;]] οἱ ἴδιοι, [[43-john.1.11|Jhn.1:11]] (M, _Pr._, 90f.; Field, _Notes_, 84) 13:1, [[44-acts.4.23|Act.4:23]], [[54-1-timothy.5.8|1Ti.5:8]]; τὰ ἴδια, one's _home_ (Field, _Notes_, l.with), [[42-luke.18.28|Luk.18:28]], [[43-john.1.11|Jhn.1:11 16:32 19:27]]. 
2. **peculiar, distinct, appropriate, proper**: τὸ ἴ. σῶμα, [[46-1-corinthians.15.38|1Co.15:38;]] ἐν τ. ἰ. τάγματι, [[46-1-corinthians.15.23|1Co.15:23;]] εἰς τ. τόπον τ. ἴ., [[44-acts.1.25|Act.1:25;]] = αὐτοῦ (see Deiss., ut. supr.), [[40-matthew.22.5|Mat.22:5]], [[43-john.1.42|Jhn.1:42]] (cf. Wis.10:1). 
3. Adverbially (see supr., 1 (_a_); and cf. WM, 739:2); 
(a) ἰδίᾳ, **severally, separately**: [[46-1-corinthians.12.11|1Co.12:11;]] 
(b) κατ᾽ ἰδίαν, **apart, privately, in private**: [[40-matthew.14.13|Mat.14:13, 23 20:17]], [[41-mark.4.34|Mrk.4:34 7:33]], [[42-luke.10.23|Luk.10:23]], [[44-acts.23.19|Act.23:19]], al.
(AS)

2443:
**ἵνα**, 
I. _adverb_ (poët., Hom., al.), 
1. of place, **where, whither**. 
2. of circumstance, **when**. 
II. _Conjunction_, 
1. prop., final, denoting purpose or end (cl.), **that, in order that**, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (cl. also) preceded by an emphatic word ([[44-acts.19.4|Act.19:4]], [[45-romans.11.31|Rom.11:31]] (?), [[48-galatians.2.10|Gal.2:10]], al.); 
(a) with optative (so in cl. after historic tenses): after a pres., [[49-ephesians.1.17|Eph.1:17]] (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2); 
(b) with subjc.: after a pres., [[41-mark.4.21|Mrk.4:21]], [[42-luke.6.34|Luk.6:34]], [[43-john.3.15|Jhn.3:15]], [[44-acts.2.25|Act.2:25]], [[45-romans.1.11|Rom.1:11]], al.; after a pf., [[40-matthew.1.22|Mat.1:22]], [[43-john.5.23|Jhn.5:23]] [[46-1-corinthians.9.22|1Co.9:22]], al.; after an imperat. (present or aor.), [[40-matthew.7.1|Mat.7:1]], [[41-mark.11.25|Mrk.11:25]], [[43-john.10.38|Jhn.10:38]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.5|1Co.7:5]], al.; after a delib. subjc., [[41-mark.1.38|Mrk.1:38]], al.; after a fut., [[42-luke.16.4|Luk.16:4]], [[43-john.14.3|Jhn.14:3]], [[46-1-corinthians.15.28|1Co.15:28]], al.; after historic tenses (where optative in cl.; WM, 359f.; M, _Pr._, 196f.), [[41-mark.6.41|Mrk.6:41]] (impf.), [[43-john.4.8|Jhn.4:8]] (plpf.), [[41-mark.3.14|Mrk.3:14]] (aor.), al.; 
(with) in late writers (M, _Pr._, 35; Burton, §§198, 199), with indic., fut: [[42-luke.20.10|Luk.20:10]], [[60-1-peter.3.1|1Pe.3:1]], al.; 
(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, see word), with indic. pres.: [[46-1-corinthians.4.6|1Co.4:6]], [[48-galatians.4.17|Gal.4:17]], al. (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.); 
(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: [[43-john.18.37|Jhn.18:37]], [[54-1-timothy.1.16|1Ti.1:16]], al.; τούτου χάριν, [[56-titus.1.5|Tit.1:5;]] 
(f) **elliptical constructions**: omission of the principal verb, [[43-john.1.8|Jhn.1:8]], [[53-2-thessalonians.3.9|2Th.3:9]], [[62-1-john.2.19|1Jn.2:19]], al.; of the final verb, [[45-romans.4.16|Rom.4:16]], [[47-2-corinthians.8.13|2Co.8:13]], al. 
2. In late writers, definitive, = inf. (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), **that**; 
(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, etc.: θέλω, [[40-matthew.7.12|Mat.7:12]], al.; ζητῶ, [[46-1-corinthians.4.2|1Co.4:2 14:12]]; ζηλόω, [[46-1-corinthians.14.1|1Co.14:1]], al.; 
(b) **after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting**: εἰπεῖν, [[40-matthew.4.3|Mat.4:3]], al.; ἐρωτῶ, [[41-mark.7.26|Mrk.7:26]], al.; παρακαλῶ, [[40-matthew.14.36|Mat.14:36]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.10|1Co.1:10]], al., etc.; 
(with) after words expressing expediency, etc.: συμφέρει, [[40-matthew.18.6|Mat.18:6]], [[43-john.11.50|Jhn.11:50]], al.; ἱκανός, [[40-matthew.8.8|Mat.8:8]], [[42-luke.7.6|Luk.7:6]]; χρείαν ἔχω, [[43-john.2.25|Jhn.2:25]], al, etc.; 
(d) **after substantives, adding further definition**: ὥρα, [[43-john.12.23|Jhn.12:23 13:1]]; χρόνος, [[66-revelation.2.21|Rev.2:21;]] συνήθεια, [[43-john.18.39|Jhn.18:39;]] μισθός, [[46-1-corinthians.9.18|1Co.9:18.]] 
3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, **that, so that** (M, _Pr._, 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): [[45-romans.11.11|Rom.11:11]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.29|1Co.7:29]], [[52-1-thessalonians.5.4|1Th.5:4]], al. (but see Thayer, see word); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, [[40-matthew.1.22|Mat.1:22 2:14]], [[43-john.13.18|Jhn.13:18]], al. 
(AS)

2448:
**Ἰούδα**, (a) Ἰουδαῖος, ὁ, **a Jew**: [[43-john.4.9|Jhn.4:9]], [[44-acts.18.24|Act.18:24]], [[45-romans.2.28|Rom.2:28]]; pl., [[66-revelation.2.9|Rev.2:9 3:9]]; οἱ Ἰ., [[40-matthew.2.2|Mat.2:2]], [[41-mark.7.3|Mrk.7:3]], [[43-john.2.6|Jhn.2:6]], al.; Ἰ. τε καὶ Ἕλληνες, [[44-acts.14.1|Act.14:1]], al.; κ. προσήλυτοι, [[44-acts.2.10|Act.2:10;]] ἔθνη τε κ. Ἰ., [[44-acts.14.5|Act.14:5;]] οἱ κατὰ τὰ ἔθνη, [[44-acts.21.21|Act.21:21;]] of Jewish Christians, [[48-galatians.2.13|Gal.2:13;]] of the ruling class who opposed Jesus, [[43-john.1.19|Jhn.1:19 2:18 5:10 11:8 13:33]], al.; 
(b) Ἰουδαία, -ας, ἡ (sc. γῆ, χώρα, cf. [[43-john.3.22|Jhn.3:22]], [[41-mark.1.5|Mrk.1:5]]), (Heb. יְהוּדָה), **Judæa**: [[40-matthew.2.1|Mat.2:1]], [[42-luke.1.5|Luk.1:5]], [[43-john.4.3|Jhn.4:3]], al.
(AS)

2532:
**καί**, 
_conj._, 
**and** 
I. Copulative. 
1. Connecting single words; 
(a) **in general**: [[40-matthew.2.18|Mat.2:18, 16:1]], [[41-mark.2.15|Mrk.2:15]], [[42-luke.8.15|Luk.8:15]], [[58-hebrews.1.1|Heb.1:1]], al. mult.; repeated before each of the terms in a series, [[40-matthew.23.23|Mat.23:23]], [[42-luke.14.21|Luk.14:21]], [[45-romans.7.12|Rom.7:12, 9:4]], al.
(b) **connecting numerals **(WM, §37, 4): [[43-john.2.20|Jhn.2:20]], [[44-acts.13.20|Act.13:20]]; 
(with) **joining terms which are not mutually exclusive, as the part with the whole**: [[40-matthew.8.33|Mat.8:33, 26:59]], [[41-mark.16.17|Mrk.16:17]], [[44-acts.5.29|Act.5:29]], al. 
2. **Connecting clauses and sentences**: [[40-matthew.3.12|Mat.3:12]], [[44-acts.5.21|Act.5:21]], al. mult.; esp. 
(a) **where, after the simplicity of the popular language, sentences are paratactically joined **(WM, §60, 3; M, _Pr._, 12; Deiss., _LAE_, 128ff.): [[40-matthew.1.21|Mat.1:21, 7:25]], [[41-mark.9.5|Mrk.9:5]], [[43-john.10.3|Jhn.10:3]], al.; 
(b) **joining affirmative to negative sentences**: [[42-luke.3.14|Luk.3:14]], [[43-john.4.11|Jhn.4:11]], IIIJhn.10; 
(with) consecutive, **and so**: [[40-matthew.5.1|Mat.5:1, 23:32]], [[58-hebrews.3.19|Heb.3:19]], al.; after imperatives, [[40-matthew.4.19|Mat.4:19]], [[42-luke.7.7|Luk.7:7]], al.; 
(d) = καίτοι, **and yet**: [[40-matthew.3.14|Mat.3:14, 6:26]], [[41-mark.12.12|Mrk.12:12]], [[42-luke.18.7|Luk.18:7]] (Field, _Notes_, 72), [[46-1-corinthians.5.2|1Co.5:2]], al.; 
(e) beginning an apodosis (= Heb. וְ; so sometimes δέ in cl.), **then**: [[42-luke.2.21|Luk.2:21, 7:12]], [[44-acts.1.10|Act.1:10]]; beginning a question (WM, §53, 3a): [[41-mark.10.26|Mrk.10:26]], [[42-luke.10.29|Luk.10:29]], [[43-john.9.36|Jhn.9:36]].
3. Epexegetic, **and, and indeed, namely** (WM, §53, 3c): [[42-luke.3.18|Luk.3:18]], [[43-john.1.16|Jhn.1:16]], [[44-acts.23.6|Act.23:6]], [[45-romans.1.5|Rom.1:5]], [[46-1-corinthians.3.5|1Co.3:5]], al.
4. **In transition**: [[40-matthew.4.23|Mat.4:23]], [[41-mark.5.1|Mrk.5:1, 21]], [[43-john.1.19|Jhn.1:19]], al.; so, Hebraistically, καὶ ἐγένετο (וַי:הִי; also ἐγένετο δέ), [[41-mark.1.9|Mrk.1:9]] (cf. [[42-luke.5.1|Luk.5:1;]] V. Burton, §§357-60; M, _Pr._, 14, 16). 
5. καὶ . . . καί, **both . . . and** (for τε . . . καί, see: τε); 
(a) **connecting single words**: [[40-matthew.10.28|Mat.10:28]], [[41-mark.4.41|Mrk.4:41]], [[45-romans.11.33|Rom.11:33]], al.; 
(b) **clauses and sentences**: [[41-mark.9.13|Mrk.9:13]], [[43-john.7.28|Jhn.7:28]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.22|1Co.1:22]], al. 
II. Adjunctive, **also, even, still**: [[40-matthew.5.39|Mat.5:39, 40]]; [[41-mark.2.28|Mrk.2:28]], al. mult.; esp. with pron., adv., etc., [[40-matthew.20.4|Mat.20:4]], [[43-john.7.47|Jhn.7:47]], al; ὡς κ., [[44-acts.11.17|Act.11:17;]] καθὼς κ., [[45-romans.15.7|Rom.15:7;]] οὑτω κ., [[45-romans.6.11|Rom.6:11;]] διὸ κ., [[42-luke.1.35|Luk.1:35;]] ὁ κ. (Deiss., _BS_, 313ff.), [[44-acts.13.9|Act.13:9;]] pleonastically, μετὰ κ.. (Bl., §77, 7; Deiss., _BS_, 265f,), [[50-philippians.4.3|Php.4:3;]] τί κ., [[46-1-corinthians.15.29|1 Co 15:29]]; ἀλλὰ κ., Luk.14:22, [[43-john.5.18|Jhn.5:18]], al.; καίγε (M, _Pr._, 230; Burton, §437), [[44-acts.17.27|Act.17:27;]] καίπερ, [[58-hebrews.5.8|Heb.5:8;]] κ. ἐάν, see: ἐάν.
**ἐάν**, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν, 
_conditional particle_, 
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. [[43-john.13.17|Jhn.13:17]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.36|1Co.7:36]]), **if haply, if**; 
1. with subjc. (cl.); 
(a) pres.: [[40-matthew.6.22|Mat.6:22]], [[42-luke.10.6|Luk.10:6]], [[43-john.7.17|Jhn.7:17]], [[45-romans.2.25|Rom.2:25, 26]] al.; 
{ (b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): [[40-matthew.4.9|Mat.4:9 16:26]] (cf. ptcp. in [[42-luke.9.25|Luk.9:25;]] M, _Pr._, 230), [[41-mark.3.24|Mrk.3:24]], [[42-luke.14.34|Luk.14:34]], [[43-john.5.43|Jhn.5:43]], [[45-romans.7.2|Rom.7:2]], al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., [[43-john.9.22|Jhn.9:22 11:57]], [[44-acts.9.2|Act.9:2]]; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, [[43-john.12.32|Jhn.12:32 14:3]], I [[43-john.2.28|Jhn.2:28 3:2]], [[58-hebrews.3.7|Heb.3:7]]" (LXX) . 
2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, _App._, 171; VD, _MGr._ 2, _App._, §77; Deiss., _BS_, 201f., _LAE_, 155, 254; M, _Pr._, 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4); 
(a) fut.: [[40-matthew.18.19|Mat.18:19]] T, [[42-luke.19.40|Luk.19:40]], [[44-acts.7.7|Act.7:7;]] 
(b) pres.: [[52-1-thessalonians.3.8|1Th.3:8]] (see Milligan, in l.). 
3. **With other particles**: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), [[48-galatians.6.1|Gal.6:1;]] ἐ. μή (M, _Pr._, 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., [[40-matthew.10.13|Mat.10:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.8.8|1Co.8:8]], [[59-james.2.17|Jas.2:17]], [[62-1-john.3.21|1Jn.3:21;]] aor., [[40-matthew.6.15|Mat.6:15]], [[41-mark.3.27|Mrk.3:27]], [[43-john.3.3|Jhn.3:3]], [[45-romans.10.15|Rom.10:15]], [[48-galatians.1.8|Gal.1:8 2:16]] (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, [[17-esther.19.13|Est.19:13]], al.,] [[45-romans.14.8|Rom.14:8]]. 
4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., _Pr._, 96; WH, _App._, 173; M, _Pr._, 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., _BS_, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., [[40-matthew.5.19|Mat.5:19]], [[41-mark.6.22|Mrk.6:22, 23]] [[42-luke.17.32|Luk.17:32]], [[46-1-corinthians.6.18|1Co.6:18]], al.; ὅπου ἐ., [[40-matthew.8.19|Mat.8:19;]] ὁσάκις ἐ., [[66-revelation.11.6|Rev.11:6;]] οὗ ἐ., [[46-1-corinthians.16.6|1Co.16:6;]] καθὸ ἐ., [[47-2-corinthians.8.12|2Co.8:12;]] ὅστις ἐ., [[48-galatians.5.10|Gal.5:10.]] 
(AS)

2563:
**κάλαμος**, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX chiefly for קָנֶה, [[23-isaiah.42.3|Isa.42:3]], [[26-ezekiel.40.3|Eze.40:3]] ff., al. ;] 
**a reed**: [[40-matthew.11.7|Mat.11:7 12:20]]" (LXX) [[42-luke.7.24|Luk.7:24;]] hence, accusative, to its various uses, 
