2596:
**κατά** (bef. a vowel κατ᾽, καθ᾽; on the frequently neglect of elision, see Tdf., _Pr._, 95; WH, _App._, 146a), 
_prep. with genitive, accusative, _ 
**down, downwards**. 
I. C. genitive (WM, §47, k; Bl., §42, 2). 
1. C. genitive of thing(s), in local sense; 
(a) **down, down from**: [[40-matthew.8.32|Mat.8:32]], [[41-mark.5.13|Mrk.5:13]], [[42-luke.8.33|Luk.8:33]], [[46-1-corinthians.11.4|1Co.11:4]]; 
(b) **throughout** (late usage; Bl, l.with): κ. ὅλης κ.τ.λ., [[42-luke.4.14|Luk.4:14 23:5]], [[44-acts.9.31|Act.9:31 10:37]]; 
(with) **in a peculiar adjectival phrase**: ἡ κ. βάθους, deep or extreme poverty, [[47-2-corinthians.8.2|2Co.8:2.]] 
2. C. genitive of person(s), usually in hostile sense; 
(a) **against** (in cl. only after verbs of speaking, witnessing, etc.): opposite to ὑπέρ, [[41-mark.9.40|Mrk.9:40;]] μετά, [[40-matthew.12.30|Mat.12:30;]] after ἐπιθυμεῖν, [[48-galatians.5.17|Gal.5:17;]] λαλεῖν, [[44-acts.6.13|Act.6:13;]] διδάσκειν, [[44-acts.21.28|Act.21:28;]] ψεύδεσθαι, [[59-james.3.14|Jas.3:14;]] after verbs of accusing, etc., [[40-matthew.5.23|Mat.5:23]], [[42-luke.23.14|Luk.23:14]], [[45-romans.8.33|Rom.8:33]], al.; verbs of fighting, prevailing, etc., [[40-matthew.10.35|Mat.10:35]], [[44-acts.14.2|Act.14:2]], [[46-1-corinthians.4.6|1Co.4:6]], al.; 
(b) of swearing, **by**: όμνυμι κ. (BL, §34, 1), [[58-hebrews.6.13|He 6:13,16]], cf. [[40-matthew.26.63|Mat.26:63.]] 
II. C. accusative (WM, §49d; BL, §42, 2). 
1. **Of motion or direction**; 
(a) **through, throughout**: [[42-luke.8.39|Luk.8:39 9:6 10:4]], [[44-acts.8.1|Act.8:1, 36]] al.; 
(b) **to, towards, over against**: [[42-luke.10.32|Luk.10:32]] (Field, _Notes_, 62), [[44-acts.2.1|Act.2:1]]o 16:7, [[48-galatians.2.11|Gal.2:11]], [[50-philippians.3.14|Php.3:14]], al.; 
(with) in adverbial phrases, **at, in, by, of**: κατ᾽ οἶκον, **at home**, [[44-acts.2.46|Act.2:46;]] κατ᾽ ἰδίαν (see: ἴδιος); καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, [[44-acts.28.16|Act.28:16]], [[45-romans.14.22|Rom.14:22]], [[59-james.2.17|Jas.2:17]]; with pron. of person(s), [[44-acts.17.28|Act.17:28 18:15]], [[45-romans.1.15|Rom.1:15]], [[49-ephesians.1.15|Eph.1:15]], al. 
2. Of time, **at, during, about**: [[44-acts.8.26|Act.8:26 12:1 19:23]], [[45-romans.9.9|Rom.9:9]] [[58-hebrews.1.10|Heb.1:10]], al. 
3. **Distributive**; 
(a) **of place**: κ. τόποὐς, [[40-matthew.24.7|Mat.24:7]], al.; κ. πόλιν, [[42-luke.8.1|Luk.8:1]], 4 al.; κ. ἐκκλησίαν, [[44-acts.14.23|Act.14:23.]] 
(b) **of time**: κ. ἔτος, [[42-luke.2.41|Luk.2:41;]] ἑορτήν, [[40-matthew.27.15|Mat.27:15]], al.; 
(with) of numbers, etc.: καθ᾽ ἕνα πάντες, [[46-1-corinthians.14.31|1Co.14:31]] (on καθ᾽ εἷς, see: εἷς); κ. ἑκατόν, [[41-mark.6.40|Mrk.6:40;]] κ. μέρος, [[58-hebrews.9.5|Heb.9:5;]] κ. ὄνομα, [[43-john.10.3|Jhn.10:3.]] 
4. Of fitness, reference, conformity, etc.; 
(a) **in relation to, concerning**: [[45-romans.1.3|Rom.1:3, 4 7:22 9:3, 5]], [[46-1-corinthians.12.6|1Co.12:6 10:18]], [[50-philippians.1.12|Php.1:12]]; κ. πάντα, [[44-acts.17.22|Act.17:22]], [[51-colossians.3.20|Col.3:20, 22]] [[58-hebrews.2.17|Heb.2:17 4:15]]; 
(b) **according to, after, like**: [[41-mark.7.5|Mrk.7:5]], [[42-luke.2.27|Luk.2:27, 29]] [[43-john.7.24|Jhn.7:24]] [[45-romans.8.4|Rom.8:4 14:15]], [[49-ephesians.2.2|Eph.2:2]], [[51-colossians.2.8|Col.2:8]], [[59-james.2.8|Jas.2:8]], al. 
III. In composition, κ. denotes, 
1. **down, down from** (καταβαίνω), etc.), hence, metaphorically; 
(a) **victory or rule over **(καταδουλόω, -κυριεύω, etc.); 
(b) "perfective" action (M, _Pr._, 111ff.). 
2. **under** (κατακαλύπτω), etc.). 
3. **in succession** (καθεξῆς). 
4. **after, behind** (καταλείπω). 
5. Hostility, **against** (καταλαλέω). 
(AS)

