2799:
**κλαίω **
[in LXX chiefly for בָּכָה ;] 
of any loud expression of pain or sorrow, esp. for the dead, to weep, lament; 
(a) intrans.: [[41-mark.5.38|Mrk.5:38-39 14:72]] (M, _Pr._, 131) [[41-mark.16.10|Mrk.16:10]], [[42-luke.7.13|Luk.7:13, 32 7:38 8:52]], [[43-john.11.31|Jhn.11:31, 33 16:20 20:11, 13 20:15]] [[44-acts.9.39|Act.9:39 21:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.30|1Co.7:30]], [[50-philippians.3.18|Php.3:18]], [[59-james.4.9|Jas.4:9 5:1]], [[66-revelation.5.5|Rev.5:5 18:15, 19]]; πολύ, [[66-revelation.5.4|Rev.5:4;]] πολλά, [[44-acts.8.24|Act.8:24]] (WH, mg.); πικρῶς, [[40-matthew.26.75|Mat.26:75]], [[42-luke.22.62|Luk.22:62]]; opposite to γελάω, [[42-luke.6.21|Luk.6:21, 25]]; χαίρω, [[45-romans.12.15|Rom.12:15;]] before ἐπί, with accusative, [[42-luke.19.41|Luk.19:41 23:28]], [[66-revelation.18.9|Rev.18:9]]; 
(b) trans., with accusative of person(s), **to weep or lament for, bewail**: [[40-matthew.2.18|Mat.2:18.]]
_SYN._: see: δακρύω (AS)

2822:
**κλητός**, -ή, -όν
(καλέω), [in LXX for קָרָא, מִקְרָא, [[02-exodus.12.16|Exo.12:16]], al. ;] 
